  "details": "**Current Behvaior**:\n\nCurrently the Avatars SDK displays the \"maximum\" and \"recommended\" quantities of the various limits that determine the performance rank. These values are basically useless unless you are planning on making a Poor ranked avatar.\n\n**Current Workaround**:\n\nRealistically this means that a creator must open the documentation webpage to find out the actual maximum quantities allowed per rank. It goes something along the lines of:\n\n1. Creator wants to target medium rank.\n\n2. SDK only shows \"maximum\" (aka poor) and \"recommended\" (aka excellent), not very helpful.\n\n3. Creator has to open documentation webpage to find the actual limits.\n\n**Desired Behavior**:\n\nThe SDK should show the limits relative to the current ranking of that item. For instance the SDK should show: \"17/16 Physbone components, Rating: Poor (maximum: 32)\", indicating that the avatar has one too many physbones to meet the next lowest performance rank (poor->medium in this example). Here the \"maximum\" should also reflect the maximum for the current rank (instead of always 1 below very poor).\n\nThis way the creator has all the information they need without having to open the and sift through documentation website.",
